cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below, and cite the models and datasets it builds on (references)."
title: "Rescue Router: few-shot flood mapping from drone photos and rescue routes on the predicted map"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Melis
    given-names: Marlen
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/MarlenMM/rescue-router"
keywords:
  - flood mapping
  - few-shot segmentation
  - disaster response
  - routing
  - drone imagery
abstract: >-
  Chameleon (a few-shot dense-prediction generalist) adapted with 50 labelled FloodNet drone photos to clear road,
  flooded road, flooded and dry building and water, a truck / boat / on-foot router on 4x4-pixel cells with vehicle
  widths and confidence tiers, a web viewer and a same-label-budget comparison with a standard fine-tuned segmenter
  (DeepLabV3-ResNet50). Research and teaching code; not for operational rescue decisions (MODEL_CARD.md).
